a:532:{s:21:"VPL_COMPILATIONFAILED";s:54:"The compilation or preparation of execution has failed";s:5:"about";s:5:"About";s:18:"acceptcertificates";s:42:"Ignore execution server certificate errors";s:30:"acceptcertificates_description";s:250:"Checking this option will allow encrypted connections to execution servers even if
their certificate is not trusted.
For security reasons, this is not recommended for production environments,
but it can be useful for testing and development purposes.";s:13:"activity_mode";s:13:"Activity mode";s:21:"activity_mode_basedon";s:8:"Based on";s:26:"activity_mode_basedon_help";s:161:"This mode indicates that the activity is to be used as a template for other activities to inherit from.<br>It also prevents students from accessing the activity.";s:18:"activity_mode_help";s:667:"Change the access rules and behavior of the activity. The modes are:
<ul>
<li><b>Normal</b>: No changes to the default behavior.</li>
<li><b>No students</b>: This mode prevents students from accessing the activity.</li>
<li><b>Students read-only</b>: This mode <b>grants</b> students access the activity in readonly mode.</li>
<li><b>Based on</b>: The activity is a template to be inherited by other activities plus "No students" mode.</li>
<li><b>VPL question</b>: The activity is adapted for use in the VPL question type, prevents students from accessing the activity.</li>
<li><b>Example</b>: The students can run and debug requested files but readonly.</li>
</ul>";s:25:"activity_mode_no_students";s:11:"No students";s:30:"activity_mode_no_students_help";s:129:"This mode prevents students from accessing the activity.<br>Regardless of other settings, students will not be able to access it.";s:20:"activity_mode_normal";s:6:"Normal";s:25:"activity_mode_normal_help";s:65:"This is the default mode, no changes to the default behavior.<br>";s:31:"activity_mode_students_readonly";s:18:"Students read-only";s:36:"activity_mode_students_readonly_help";s:185:"This mode grants students access to the activity in read-only mode.<br>Regardless of other settings, students can view the activity and its content, but they cannot edit or submit code.";s:25:"activity_mode_vplquestion";s:12:"VPL question";s:30:"activity_mode_vplquestion_help";s:130:"This mode is used to adapt the activity for use in the VPL question type.<br>It prevents students from accessing the activity.<br>";s:7:"addfile";s:8:"Add file";s:11:"addoverride";s:15:"Add an override";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Advanced";s:8:"allfiles";s:9:"All files";s:14:"allsubmissions";s:15:"All submissions";s:13:"always_use_ws";s:46:"Always use unencrypted (ws) websocket protocol";s:14:"always_use_wss";s:45:"Always use encrypted (wss) websocket protocol";s:7:"anyfile";s:8:"Any file";s:7:"archive";s:11:"ZIP archive";s:14:"archivereplace";s:37:"Replace only files present in archive";s:20:"archivereplacedelete";s:57:"Replace all files and delete files not present in archive";s:13:"attemptnumber";s:19:"Attempt number {$a}";s:10:"autodetect";s:10:"Autodetect";s:19:"automaticevaluation";s:20:"Automatic evaluation";s:16:"automaticgrading";s:15:"Automatic grade";s:21:"automaticgrading_help";s:248:"If set to Yes, the grade proposed by the automatic evaluation will be applied as the grade for this activity.<br>
