This action will only fill the form, no data will be submitted.";s:17:"inconsistentgroup";s:46:"You are not member of only one group (0 or >1)";s:24:"incorrect_directory_name";s:24:"Incorrect directory name";s:19:"incorrect_file_name";s:19:"Incorrect file name";s:24:"indicator:cognitivedepth";s:13:"VPL cognitive";s:29:"indicator:cognitivedepth_help";s:88:"This indicator is based on the cognitive depth reached by the student in a VPL activity.";s:23:"indicator:socialbreadth";s:10:"VPL social";s:28:"indicator:socialbreadth_help";s:87:"This indicator is based on the social breadth reached by the student in a VPL activity.";s:14:"individualwork";s:15:"Individual work";s:16:"inheritancechain";s:18:"Inheritance chain:";s:12:"inheritvalue";s:14:"Inherit ({$a})";s:11:"inputoutput";s:12:"Input/Output";s:17:"instanceselection";s:13:"VPL selection";s:12:"intermediate";s:12:"Intermediate";s:9:"isexample";s:7:"Example";s:14:"isexample_help";s:106:"This activity acts as an example, allowing students to run and debug the example files, but not to submit.";s:12:"jail_servers";s:22:"Execution servers list";s:19:"jail_servers_config";s:24:"Execution servers config";s:24:"jail_servers_description";s:28:"Write a line for each server";s:11:"joinedfiles";s:21:"Joined selected files";s:15:"keepcurrentfile";s:17:"Keep current file";s:9:"keepfiles";s:26:"Files to keep when running";s:14:"keepfiles_help";s:245:"<p>Due to security issues, the files added as &quot;Execution files&quot; are deleted before running the file vpl_execution.</p>
If any of those files is needed during the execution (for example, to be used as test data), it must be marked here.";s:10:"keybinding";s:11:"Key binding";s:8:"keyboard";s:8:"Keyboard";s:9:"lasterror";s:15:"Last error info";s:13:"lasterrordate";s:15:"Last error date";s:14:"listofcomments";s:16:"List of comments";s:5:"lists";s:5:"Lists";s:14:"listsimilarity";s:26:"List of similarities found";s:14:"listwatermarks";s:15:"Watermarks list";s:18:"liveautocompletion";s:19:"Live autocompletion";s:4:"load";s:4:"Load";s:7:"loading";s:7:"Loading";s:18:"local_jail_servers";s:23:"Local execution servers";s:23:"local_jail_servers_help";s:562:"<p>Here you can set the local execution servers added for this activity and those
that are based on it.</p>
<p>Enter the full URL of a server on each line. You can use blank lines
and comments starting the line with "#".</p>
<p>This activity will use as execution server list: the servers set here
plus the server list set in the "based on" activity
plus the list of common execution servers.
If you want to prevent this activity and derived ones
from using other servers, then you have to add a line
containing "end_of_jails" at the end of the server list.
</p>";s:13:"manualgrading";s:14:"Manual grading";s:4:"math";s:4:"Math";s:14:"maxexefilesize";s:27:"Maximum execution file size";s:12:"maxexememory";s:19:"Maximum memory used";s:15:"maxexeprocesses";s:27:"Maximum number of processes";s:10:"maxexetime";s:22:"Maximum execution time";s:8:"maxfiles";s:23:"Maximum number of files";s:16:"maxfilesexceeded";s:32:"Maximum number of files exceeded";s:11:"maxfilesize";s:24:"Maximum upload file size";s:19:"maxfilesizeexceeded";s:26:"Maximum file size exceeded";s:13:"maximumperiod";s:19:"Maximum period {$a}";s:19:"maxpostsizeexceeded";s:76:"Maximum server post size exceeded. Please, remove files or reduce files size";s:17:"maxresourcelimits";s:34:"Maximum execution resources limits";s:19:"maxsimilarityoutput";s:28:"Maximum output by similarity";s:22:"menucheck_jail_servers";s:23:"Check execution servers";s:18:"menuexecutionfiles";s:15:"Execution files";s:20:"menuexecutionoptions";s:7:"Options";s:13:"menukeepfiles";s:13:"Files to keep";s:22:"menulocal_jail_servers";s:23:"Local execution servers";s:18:"menuresourcelimits";s:16:"Resources limits";s:5:"merge";s:11:"Merge grade";s:10:"merge_help";s:686:"Merge current proposed grade (from execution) and advanced grading grid grade.
<p>
This will set the grade to
&lt;proposed&nbsp;grade&gt; - &lt;max&nbsp;grid&nbsp;points&gt; * (&lt;proposed&nbsp;grade&gt;/&lt;max&nbsp;vpl&nbsp;grade&gt;) + &lt;grid&nbsp;points&gt;.<br>
More simply, it ponderates grid points based on current proposed grade: a student with 100% points will need all grid points to keep 100% points;
a student with 0 points will end up with all obtained grid points as their grade.
</p>
<p>
Advanced grid grade is computed as the total of grid points, reduced by comments. Syntax for grade reduction is <pre>-&nbsp;Text&nbsp;(-points)</pre> (one line by reduction).
</p>";s:23:"message::bad_jailserver";s:79:"Not used due server software update required. Contact your system administrator";s:36:"message::body_footer_bad_jailservers";s:352:"
To download the latest version of the VPL-Jail-System,
visit the VPL for Moodle home page and navigate to the "Download" section.
Remember to use the parameters URLPATH and/or TASK_ONLY_FROM
to enhance your security settings as recommended.

To locate activities using local VPL Jail servers,
search in the field jailservers of the table {prefix}vpl.
";s:36:"message::body_header_bad_jailservers";s:101:"
The VPL Jail servers in the following list
**urgently** need to update the VPL-Jail-System software:";s:32:"message::subject_bad_jailservers";s:65:"Important Report of the VPL Plugin in Moodle on the '{$a}' Server";s:31:"messageprovider:bad_jailservers";s:23:"Report VPL Jail Servers";s:11:"minsimlevel";s:32:"Minimum similarity level to show";s:17:"moduleconfigtitle";s:17:"VPL Module Config";s:10:"modulename";s:23:"Virtual programming lab";s:15:"modulename_help";s:519:"<p>VPL is an activity module for Moodle that manages programming assignments and whose salient features are:
</p>
<ul>
<li>Enable to edit the programs source code in the browser</li>
<li>Students can run interactively programs in the browser</li>
<li>You can run tests to review the programs.</li>
<li>Allows searching for similarity between files.</li>
<li>Allows setting editing restrictions and avoiding external text pasting.</li>
</ul>
